alex_dx: Heads up — customer reported: importing SDK in app/layout.tsx breaks Edge build with: "ReferenceError: crypto is not defined".

 tina_ing: Likely CJS fallback hitting node crypto poly. How is the package resolving? main/module/exports?

 alex_dx: package.json has "main": "dist/index.cjs.js", "module": "dist/index.esm.js", no "exports" block. Next picks cjs sometimes.

 omar_ts: For Next + app router, we usually need an explicit exports map so bundlers don't pick the CJS entry for edge. Quick local hack: in next.config.js alias to the ESM file:
```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config) => {
    config.resolve.alias = config.resolve.alias || {};
    config.resolve.alias['redwood-inference'] = require('path').resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules/redwood-inference/dist/index.esm.js');
    return config;
  }
};
```
Works but ugly.

 ci-bot: Note: PR 842 proposed adding "exports" map for edge/browser entries.

 alex_dx: Also running into TypeScript annoyance: when I do dynamic import inside a client component TS complains: "Cannot use import statement outside a module" at compile time even though runtime fine.

 tina_ing: Use types-only import: `import type { ClientOptions } from 'redwood-inference';` then at runtime: `const sdk = await import('redwood-inference/dist/edge.mjs');`. For typing the dynamic import you can do: `const sdk = await import('redwood-inference') as typeof import('redwood-inference');`

 omar_ts: Another pattern: create a tiny wrapper file src/lib/rdw-edge.ts that re-exports typed bindings from the ESM build and import that wrapper everywhere. Keeps next.config changes minimal.

 alex_dx: Any long-term plan on SDK side? We should ship "exports" with conditional entrypoints: {import: './dist/index.esm.js', require: './dist/index.cjs.js', browser: './dist/edge.mjs'} and a separate types entry.

 ci-bot: Reminder: add a test matrix for Next.js (server, client, edge) in CI before cutting a release.

 tina_ing: Also watch out for SSR hydration mismatch if you do client dynamic import that changes markup on first render. Wrap in a client component and show loading state.

 alex_dx: I'll open an issue with repro and attach minimal repo. Meanwhile adding alias + types-only import fixed local build. Thanks.

 omar_ts: We'll add exports + edge build + README snippet about Next app-router + "use client"/"use server" boundaries.

 alex_dx: Perfect. filing issue + cc @maria_devex for docs.
